# Tracer: ExactIntegerQuotient
# Before: explicit proof bridge
# a=b*quot(a,b)+a%b=b*quot(a,b)
# a/b=quot(a,b)
# Old direct target missed search_proof; the explicit bridge was required in the dated probe. The old quot bridge was checked only for positive b.
# Now: direct guarded target
# Known integer leaves now compose by structural membership. This tracer
# retains the builtin fallback for a checked function-return carrier.
forall f fn(t Z) Z, a,b Z:
    b!=0
    f(a)%b=0
    =>:
        f(a)/b $in Z

# Boundary: missing guards and false conclusions remain rejected by selected_scalar_bt_rules_tests.
